n inhibition of phosphorylation of ERK1/2, AKT and signal transducers and activator of transcription 3, and the significant upregulation of FOXO1, BCL2, and BCL2L11. Accordingly, TCHHL1 is associated with survival of cutaneous SCC. In addition, we hypothesize that TCHHL1 may be a novel therapeutic target in cutaneous SCC.\n\n",
